SWEET framebuffer on a panel larger than 1125x2436 (raven 1440x3120): present 1125x2436 centred 1:1 instead of the native size, unless sweetfb_native=1. Replaces the two NOPs in AppleCLCD::start of the raven-xnu7 test kernel; panels <= 1125x2436 (sweet, bluejay) take the same path as before.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -77,6 +77,9 @@ enum {
  * rdar://45025538 bar for 360x800 points). The display is therefore
  * presented as the iPhone X panel, 1125x2436 (375x812 points @3x), and the
  * centered 1080x2400 part of it is shown on the 1080x2400 panel.
+ * A larger panel (raven, 1440x3120) gets the same 1125x2436 display, drawn
+ * 1:1 in its centre: a native 1440x3120 display got all-zero frames from
+ * backboardd (raven-xnu5, device/google/raven/hardware/ios-gui-2026-11-05.txt).
  * Boot-arg sweetfb_native=1 presents the real panel size instead.
  */
 #define SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_W              1125
@@ -219,7 +222,8 @@ AppleCLCD::start(IOService *provider)
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_native", &native, sizeof(native));
 	fLogicalW = fWidth;
 	fLogicalH = fHeight;
-	if (!native && fWidth <= SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_W && fHeight <= SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_H) {
+	/* On a larger panel fOffX/fOffY are negative: present() (dx -= fOffX) then shifts each layer into the panel's centre. */
+	if (!native) {
 		fLogicalW = SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_W;
 		fLogicalH = SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_H;
 	}
